Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-06-07
Subject: Depack daopt's in-memory TContent optimizer state
License: expat

`compiler/i386/daopt.pas` stores per-register optimizer state in the packed
`TContent` record. The optimizer passes `WState` and `RState` fields to
`IncState(var Byte)` and keeps `StartMod` pointers in the same slots.

This state is in-memory-only, not part of any file format. Keeping it packed
forces the translated bootstrap to form typed references to possibly unaligned
subfields for ordinary optimizer updates. Depack `TContent` so the bootstrap
keeps natural alignment without changing serialized compiler data.

--- a/compiler/i386/daopt.pas
+++ b/compiler/i386/daopt.pas
@@ -106,3 +106,8 @@ type
-  TContent = Packed Record
+  { was `packed record` -- depacked for the tp2cc-translated bootstrap. This
+    is in-memory optimizer state, not an on-disk format. The optimizer passes
+    WState/RState fields to var parameters and keeps StartMod pointers in the
+    same per-register slots; packing those slots would require unaligned typed
+    references for ordinary state updates. }
+  TContent = Record
       {start and end of block instructions that defines the
        content of this register.}
                StartMod: pai;
